{"title":"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the largest value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c471843498de1d9d0b05ad7f32eab45e216577b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> for pairs of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real numbers\">real numbers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> which satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4af4499d6d772ee9578a7b46151347637e4ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-3)^2+(y-3)^2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41061725e3f90dc4b08451aed479508531e9f58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }3+2\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }2+\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 3\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }6 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 6+2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"525\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5453fcb114c35f4d2d846a342183c2d0f0defe84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{x}=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd14499bebbf7855623388869c0910c4a004bf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />. Substituting this into the given <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4af4499d6d772ee9578a7b46151347637e4ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-3)^2+(y-3)^2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d0187ebdc44342743aa38f6b36755d79371f27cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-3)^2+(kx-3)^2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"19\" />. Multiplying this out and forming it into a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Quadratic\">quadratic</a> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b3773aca3e94f29d257d439044a528d9cd48c7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+k^2)x^2+(-6-6k)x+12=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>We want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real number</a>, so we must have the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant\" title=\"Discriminant\">discriminant</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f906fd7a43bf2b009d93d27db3947fcd893d001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />. \nThe discriminant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/75681d91c8d4edfa8cd6c89c3954b1e3d088d404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-6-6k)^2-4(1+k^2)(12)=36k^2+72k+36-48-48k^2=-12k^2+72k-12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"626\" height=\"19\" />. Therefore, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a14ea688ccd6da12b20d320970ae9e07ed5c0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-12k^2+72k-12\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5adf3025a884f5d64c963a07bcef324df772102e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2-6k+1\\leq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(polynomial)\" title=\"Root (polynomial)\">roots</a> of this quadratic, using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_formula\" title=\"Quadratic formula\">quadratic formula</a>, are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cb134ad844ee0ca50e55c5275819740c74024b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\pm2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, so the quadratic can be <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring\" title=\"Factoring\">factored</a> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65c089d8baedf01f4cb6e264bdda001366ba029f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-(3-2\\sqrt{2}))(k-(3+2\\sqrt{2}))\\leq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"283\" height=\"21\" />. We can now separate this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases:\n</p><p><b>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d999b32fdf300017cc1f89436ef785f8329b7bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;3-2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /></b>\nThen, both <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Term&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Term (page does not exist)\">terms</a> in the factored quadratic are negative, so the inequality doesn't hold.\n</p><p><b>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cffb0ec00cb66c6acba0aad5c01d1c630beefd17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-2\\sqrt{2}&lt;k&lt;3+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" /></b>\nThen, the first term is positive and the second is negative and the second is positive, so the inequality holds.\n</p><p><b>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea2011dd7dd5c8dba7cd788c063ef4ceecdc592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;3+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /></b>\nThen, both terms are positive, so the inequality doesn't hold.\n</p><p>Also, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba536470c1ff70983e5407d4dd4cc43839fbfb24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3-2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61540ffd6e3be44d7fb8ea212424a72d1f27dbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, the equality holds.\n</p><p>Therefore, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97ef979086f5ad7d597371367ca09299edde49d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-2\\sqrt{2}\\leq k\\leq3+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"188\" height=\"19\" />, and the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f44eec093fc38e9b00891dea67c50a9411eff84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{y}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f5ad03381a3862c976e2d1d9c2becd6ffeb576.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3+2\\sqrt{2}}, \\boxed{\\text{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation represents a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af834b481b16223a0f04fa9a05f4f8a581e0182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/657a5cfa533cfc358effb3e34d881a93d74050da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(3,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />. To find the maximal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd14499bebbf7855623388869c0910c4a004bf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is equivalent to finding the maximum slope of a line passing through the origin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and intersecting the circle. The steepest such line is tangent to the circle at some point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5c7c24b91e5eede7062e0c8a6a23b91d5816bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XA=\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cda9d9db23055b044630d43b5e1a1aa264d80b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA=\\sqrt{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150f029141dd8a5a1300201f037bb6585ded3447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OXA = 90$\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" /> because the line is tangent to the circle. Using the pythagorean theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10ece12eb320a2ff1b25528f6da1e2a6b546e50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX=\\sqrt{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>The slope we are looking for is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483d7a045e4cb134dc47ec512a436568b56b0a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan (\\theta + 45)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/99283c8ed3109e9f9c60a35db8f9bfef0a97b3b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOX = \\theta$\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />. Using tangent addition,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a35dacb9bb38e2c0733d4e32b6baff8fb291ff78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan (\\theta + 45)= \\frac{\\tan \\theta + \\tan 45}{1-\\tan\\theta\\tan 45} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}+1}{1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}}=3+2\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"408\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" /> is the answer\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Following the steps of Solution 2, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10ece12eb320a2ff1b25528f6da1e2a6b546e50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX=\\sqrt{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/41414e3bb78f5907a1520cad6672ac51edcf83da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = (x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. Based on the distance to the origin and to the centre of the circle\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f2efee9132f17fa76e11515b693e4b1305e0f4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + y^2 = 12\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b2f16d32e2385ee3302a50d3b8ae9ee72d4d03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x - 3)^2 + (y - 3)^2 = 6\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Expanding the latter and substituting the former into the equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c69b31f2e67131d44e1fea648adf72092c71f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 - 6(x + y) = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f37629dc5b0db0dc7655a6ef18988faa0ae552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />. We can square this and remove the 1st equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b99539612b3d9845278ddb407bc716c22edb6ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2xy = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/9779311aab441e4a55cba407f9bec73868f0030a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75ef2811845e8d169f1657dd83cf8d56150ee524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 4 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c425c24fe9fbead9383efeeeaa62d835800dc43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x(4 - x) = 2\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/7517137cf531b0eaab8522338d44279c40e9d872.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - 4x + 2 = 0\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9ef70206b32f050c28e0f79483f221756aa483a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 2 \\pm \\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are symmetric, we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be the lower number to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f87133ae5336a296b8475cbfab94f48a1612c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2 - \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba8a6f1fe0eef66c63a68543612a3dbb4997bd50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2 + \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/6598721ef4899f417b1d39313bf6f5da74e32961.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{y}{x} = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{2 - \\sqrt{2}}\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/5795c5b9ee3ad72c144367afe9e8470b49d4b5a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{y}{x} = \\frac{(2 + \\sqrt{2})^2}{2}\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557659f9fb499154bb2226434a385b6d0035c1b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{y}{x} = 3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME\" title=\"1984 AHSME\">1984 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1984 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1